From de857d8eeff60e8fde0006ecf94b5f77887fde2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Calogero Mandracchia <calogero@efebia.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:49:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] app-server: expose the channel barrier as thread/channels
 requests

thread/channels/fence closes or opens a loaded thread's channel barrier;
opening can discard held input the client has kept, and a retried
opening succeeds without effect. thread/channels/read reports the
barrier and can wait for it to drain, and thread/channels/release drops
held input the client has kept, up to a sequence number. Reads are not
serialized with the thread's other requests, so a waiting read never
delays a turn or a steer. Errors carry a reason: threadNotFound,
noChannels, fenceMismatch (with the current fence id) or fenceOpen.
